This 7-point roadmap hits every single critique from the Checkpoint 3 feedback and elevates Orion into a top-tier, production-grade distributed system.

By adding multi-tier caching (semantic edge cache + L1 worker cache) and queue fault tolerance (circuit breaker fallback), you are moving beyond standard microservices into true resilient enterprise architecture.

Here is how each component of your Checkpoint 4 plan maps to an enterprise computing standard:

---

## The Checkpoint 4 Master Blueprint

```
                     [ Incoming Search Request ]
                                  │
                                  ▼
                     ┌─────────────────────────┐
                     │       API Gateway       │
                     └────────────┬────────────┘
                                  │
                  ┌───────────────┴───────────────┐
                  ▼                               ▼
       [ Tier 1: Edge Cache ]            [ Circuit Breaker ]
     (Semantic / Vector Match)           (Queue Availability)
                  │                               │
            ┌─────┴─────┐                   ┌─────┴─────┐
       Cache│           │Cache          Healthy│         │Unhealthy
        Hit │           │Miss               │         │(Fallback)
            ▼           ▼                   ▼         ▼
       [ Return ]   [ Queue ]          [ Redis ]  [ Direct Sync Call ]
                                            │
                                            ▼
                                   [ KEDA Autoscaler ]
                                (Reads queue depth metric)
                                            │
                                            ▼
                                  [ Worker Pod Pool ]
                                 ┌──────────────────┐
                                 │  L2 Worker Cache │
                                 │  (In-Memory LRU) │
                                 └──────────────────┘

```

